        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A water heater blanket earns its place on an older tank that feels warm to the touch, sits in a cool space, and carries less than R-24 from the factory. On those tanks, the Frost King SP57/11C gives a dependable R10 for the least fuss, while the SmartJacket and AES jackets suit owners who want no fiberglass or have a very large tank.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you choose, the clearances matter more than the R-value: keep the top, burner and flue of a gas heater clear, leave electric thermostat panels and every label exposed, and read your heater's manual first. Add pipe insulation and a 120 degree thermostat setting, and you have most of the savings available short of a new heater.
          </p>
